course: dictionary
lesson: 7326
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Plane is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context.
explain: «An airport is like a huge machine for sorting people, bags and planes.» Airports, people and bags tell you that planes here means aeroplanes, machines with wings that fly.
explain: Now read «plane shapes», which are flat shapes like squares and triangles. Here plane means flat. It is the same spelling with a different meaning, so always check the clues.
fact: «Plane» as a noun can mean an aeroplane, a machine with wings that flies.
fact: In maths, a plane is a flat surface that goes on forever in all directions.
fact: A plane is also a tool for making wood smooth and flat.
fact: A plane tree is a big tree often planted in city streets.
fact: «Plane» can also be an adjective meaning flat.
exercise: «Noise-cancelling headphones work best on steady droning noise, like a train or a plane engine.» What does plane mean here? | *Aeroplane | Flat surface | Big tree | Tool for wood
exercise: In maths, «plane shapes» like squares and triangles are what? | *Flat | Tall | Sharp | Hollow
exercise: The city planted a row of plane trees along the street. What is a plane tree? | *Big tree often planted in city streets | Machine with wings | Flat surface in maths | Tool for smoothing wood
test: «Flaps and slats slide out of the wing at take-off and landing, so the plane can fly slowly without falling.» What does plane mean here? | Tool for wood | Tree | Flat surface | *Aeroplane
test: Sam runs a plane over the wooden board to make it smooth. What is a plane here? | Big tree | Aeroplane | Flat shape in maths | *Tool for making wood smooth and flat
exam: Check that the table top is plane, with no bumps. What does plane mean? | *Flat | Tool for wood | Machine that flies | Big tree
